      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote",
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Purpose:\n- Professional material / surface / object replacement.\n\nInputs:\n- Image 1 = main image.\n- Image 2 = material or object reference.\n\nStarter prompt idea:\n- \"Replace the current sofa material with the fur texture from Image 2 while keeping the sofa shape, room composition, and lighting coherent.\"\n\nOrigin:\n- This corresponds to the official Qwen Image Edit 2511 material-replacement use case.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\nIdentity Preservation Rules:\n- The main person's face identity must stay stable.\n- Keep face shape, eye spacing, nose shape, mouth shape, skin characteristics, and recognizable appearance.\n- If multiple reference images are used, they may influence clothing, pose, lighting, background, or materials — not identity, unless explicitly designated as the identity reference.\n- For edits that do not require face changes, prefer keeping the face untouched or minimally changed.\n- If identity drift happens in practice, recommended recovery stack:\n  1) make Image 1 the identity anchor,\n  2) keep the prompt explicit about preserving identity,\n  3) use local/cropped editing for non-face changes,\n  4) use ReActor as a final face restore/fallback pass,\n  5) optionally use FaceDetailer with low denoise for face cleanup only.\n- Image 1 is the default identity anchor unless explicitly noted otherwise.\n\nPrompt Guard Upgrade:\n- The positive prompt is now split into:\n  1) SYSTEM PROMPT — protected identity-preserving rules\n  2) USER PROMPT — the part you edit\n- The negative prompt is also split into:\n  1) SYSTEM NEGATIVE — protected anti-drift / anti-face-mismatch rules\n  2) USER NEGATIVE — optional extra negatives\n- This prevents accidental deletion of the identity-preservation logic during normal use.\n\nFace Guard v6:\n- This workflow now includes an active post-process identity branch: ReActor face restore + FaceDetailer cleanup.\n- Identity anchor is restored after the main Qwen edit to reduce face drift.\n- If the subject is not a human face, bypass the Face Guard nodes.\n"
      ],
      "title": "07 — Object / Material Replacement — Guide & Prompt",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
